      "homepage": "https://ifcopenshell.org",
      "rationale": "IfcOpenShell 0.8.4 is the reference open-source IFC implementation and, unlike `ruststep`, it both READS and WRITES ISO 10303-21: `ifcopenshell.open` runs its own C++ Part-21 parser against the real IFC4 EXPRESS schema and `ifcopenshell.file.to_string`/`write` re-serialize the whole exchange structure from the parsed model. That makes it a genuine second PRODUCER — the role `ruststep` cannot fill — and it is registered here for exactly the differential case `../../../../🧪️tests/differential-ifc-4` that claims it. It does NOT replace `ruststep-ifc-4-any-mutate`, which stays the schema-agnostic independent READER of `mutate-ifc-4`: IfcOpenShell is schema-BOUND, so it can neither produce nor faithfully read the four kinds of this subset's vocabulary that leave the IFC4 schema. Measured on this subset's own real fixture rather than assumed — retyping `#16976` to `RENAMED_PROXY` makes `ifcopenshell.file.from_string` return 16975 of 24792 entities with no error raised, a tenth positional argument on a nine-attribute entity is read back silently dropped, and `ifcopenshell.file.remove` documents and performs reference repair (`#16976` disappears from `#16991`'s member aggregate) where `IfcMutation::RemoveEntity` deliberately does not cascade. `set-entity-name`, `insert-entity-arg`, `remove-entity-arg` and `remove-entity` are therefore NOT claimed here and carry no differential scenario; the seven kinds that are claimed are produced end to end by IfcOpenShell and re-read from its own written bytes.",
